# 🧠 Monorepo Architecture Rules

This repository follows a strict modular architecture.  
All code must respect boundaries between apps and packages.

Project structure:

- apps/api → NestJS backend
- apps/web → Next.js frontend
- packages/ui → Reusable UI components (design system)
- packages/database → Custom ORM & database entry point
- packages/common-lib → Shared cross-platform utilities
- packages/backend-lib → Backend-only shared logic
- packages/frontend-lib → Frontend-only shared logic

---

# 🔒 1. Architecture Boundaries (STRICT)

## apps/api
- Must NOT import from:
  - apps/web
  - packages/frontend-lib
  - packages/ui
- Can import:
  - packages/database
  - packages/common-lib
  - packages/backend-lib

## apps/web
- Must NOT import from:
  - apps/api
  - packages/backend-lib
- Can import:
  - packages/ui
  - packages/common-lib
  - packages/frontend-lib

## packages/ui
- Pure UI components only
- No business logic
- No API calls
- No database logic
- No environment access
- Must be reusable
- Must follow global design system

Before creating a new component:
→ ALWAYS check if it already exists in packages/ui

## packages/database
- Single source of truth for database access
- All DB logic must go here
- apps/api must not bypass this layer

## packages/common-lib
- Cross-platform pure utilities
- No framework-specific code
- No side effects
- **Single source of truth for shared types** between `apps/web` and `apps/api`
  - All shared **types/interfaces** must live in `packages/common-lib/src/types/`
  - All shared **schemas** must live in `packages/common-lib/src/schemas/`
  - Avoid creating duplicated “web-only” vs “api-only” versions of the same domain type
  - If a smaller shape is needed, prefer `Pick/Omit` from the shared type (e.g. `CompactUser`)

## packages/backend-lib
- Backend business logic
- Services, domain logic
- No direct DB access (must use database package)

## packages/frontend-lib
- Frontend domain logic
- Hooks, formatters, state helpers
- No API route definitions

