# 🧠 4. Clean Code Principles

- No duplicated logic
- No circular dependencies
- No cross-layer leaks
- Keep files small and focused
- Prefer pure functions
- Explicit return types
- Avoid `any`
- Strict TypeScript always
- **No hardcoded important values** (thresholds, statuses, tokens, enums, app-wide rules)
  - Prefer constants/enums from shared sources:
    - `packages/common-lib/src/constants/constants.ts`
    - `packages/common-lib/src/constants/enums.ts`
  - API-only constants live in:
    - `apps/api/src/common/utils/constants.ts`
  - When adding a new “important” constant, put it in the right constants file (don’t inline magic numbers/strings)

Folder structure must reflect domain boundaries.

